@namespace
#throughout this code, i utilise class and def functions, to categorise the sprites, which are the interactable objects and characters
#and to group events which will happen in the game together
#I use strings and the equivalent of print functions through makecode aracde's story extension
#to display text on screen
#and I use integers, which are numerical digits, to set speed, map positions, time durations and count score
#occasionaly I also make use of boolean operators, True and False, to make the distinction between the game ending as a Loss or a Win, and to determine when an act or animation should occur.
class SpriteKind: #Here I'm using the class function to create and define the different kinds of characters and interactable objects in the game.
    npc = SpriteKind.create()
    door = SpriteKind.create()
    book1 = SpriteKind.create()
    librarian = SpriteKind.create()
    englisht = SpriteKind.create()
    matht = SpriteKind.create()
    sciencet = SpriteKind.create()
    bookeng = SpriteKind.create()
    bookmath = SpriteKind.create()
    booksci = SpriteKind.create() #some of these names are not grouped together, such as just having books, this is because later on, the events on interaction with each book will differ, so I must differentiate them now to easily identify then.
@namespace
class StatusBarKind:
    progress = StatusBarKind.create()

